From: k4 <k4@local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: backport BPF_MAP_TYPE_RINGBUF (user-space side) to 5.4

Android 17's Tethering mainline module (libservice-connectivity.so:
LocalNetEventListener / LoopbackEventHandler) opens pinned BPF ring buffer
maps, checks the map type, mmap()s the consumer page (rw) and the producer +
data pages (ro) and epoll()s the fd; without the map type system_server
aborts. This adds the map type with upstream semantics:

- uapi: BPF_MAP_TYPE_STRUCT_OPS (26, placeholder, not implemented) and
  BPF_MAP_TYPE_RINGBUF (27) so the numbering matches upstream v5.8+, plus the
  BPF_RINGBUF_{BUSY_BIT,DISCARD_BIT,HDR_SZ} record-header constants.
- kernel/bpf/ringbuf.c from upstream 457f44363a88 (v5.8): allocation
  (max_entries power of 2 and page aligned, key/value size 0, only
  BPF_F_NUMA_NODE), data pages double-mapped via vmap(), mmap() and poll().
  Includes upstream fixes 04ea3086c4d7 (v5.13, CVE-2021-3489: only the
  consumer page may be mapped writable, VM_MAYWRITE cleared otherwise) and
  b293dcc473d2 (VM_MAP instead of VM_ALLOC for the vmap area).
- bpf_map_ops gains ->map_mmap() and ->map_poll(); bpf_map_fops gains
  .mmap/.poll (bpf_map_mmap()/bpf_map_poll() from upstream fc9702273e2e
  v5.5 and 457f44363a88): MAP_SHARED only, VM_MAYEXEC dropped, read-only
  mappings cannot be mprotect()ed writable, maps without ->map_poll() return
  EPOLLERR like upstream. Only ringbuf implements ->map_mmap() (array mmap /
  BPF_F_MMAPABLE is not backported), so the writecnt/freeze_mutex bookkeeping
  of fc9702273e2e is not needed; a frozen map still refuses PROT_WRITE.
- The new enum values and bpf_map_ops members are hidden from genksyms
  (#ifndef __GENKSYMS__) and appended at the end, so no exported symbol CRC
  (CONFIG_MODVERSIONS) and no existing struct member offset changes.

Not backported: the BPF-side producer helpers bpf_ringbuf_output/reserve/
submit/discard/query and their verifier support. The verifier rejects every
helper call on a ringbuf map, so programs cannot touch it and the ring stays
empty on this kernel (readers never get EPOLLIN).

